Skia

paint/glyph.rs follows Skia's quadratic subdivision (cheap_distance and
diff_to_shift in src/core/SkEdge.cpp). The code was ported from the Rust
port of those two functions in tiny-skia 0.11.4, src/edge.rs (crates.io),
and keeps their integer arithmetic with accuracy shift 2.

The 8 mask gamma tables in paint/glyph.rs follow Skia's preblend gamma,
apply_contrast and the correcting LUT of src/core/SkMaskGamma.cpp. They
were generated in f32 with contrast 0.2, power gamma 1.2 and source
luminance (i << 5) | (i << 2) | (i >> 1) for i in 0 to 7. The formula was
written from SkMaskGamma.cpp; no Skia revision was recorded at the time.
The unit test in paint/glyph.rs regenerates all 8 tables from it.

